#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064009 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236f51c2-22ad-551f-afb4-62fd6de6d21e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Quotient of Linear Polynomials"}] :question/id #uuid "4d4edfc8-e178-58b4-b827-e4310ead130e" :question/math-academy-id "e-485" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_0^1 \\dfrac{4x-1}{x+1}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color{red}-1$ | $4$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $-4$ |\n|  | $4$ | $-5$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4x-1}{x+1} = 4 -\\dfrac{5}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{4x-1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(4-\\frac{5}{x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4\\,\\text{d}x-5{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4x{|}_{0}^{1}-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[4-0]-5[\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1] \\\\  & =4-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064010 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f110daa3-fd31-5e34-8a88-0e002c2e418a" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator is Linear"}] :question/id #uuid "74761123-d539-5d78-8dcd-4ea1db04bed0" :question/math-academy-id "e-486" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{2x^2-3x-4}{x-3}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division. \n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n|  | $x^2$ | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color{red}3$ | $2$ | $-3$ | $-4$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $6$ | $9$ |\n|  | $2$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac{ 2x^2-3x-4}{x-3} = 2x + 3 + \\dfrac {5}{x-3} .\n\t}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2{x}^{2}-3x-4}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+3+\\frac{5}{x-3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+3x+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064011 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator Contains a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/id #uuid "cf016fa7-c3a2-5f9b-84a6-7b005d0d7286" :question/math-academy-id "e-487" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{x-1}{2x-1}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $2$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-1}{2x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{x-1}{2(x-\\frac{1}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{x-1}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n|  | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color{red}\\dfrac12$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $\\dfrac12$ |\n|  | $1$ | $-\\dfrac12$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-1}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})} & =1-\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{2(x-\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{2x-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-1}{2x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (1-\\frac{1}{2x-1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|]+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314861 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f110daa3-fd31-5e34-8a88-0e002c2e418a" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator is Linear"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fc6059b-7293-5aa3-92c7-3092e97eca56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+x+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314863} {:answer/id #uuid "f349a1f0-879b-5869-97b3-7beded281852" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{2}+x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314864} {:answer/id #uuid "a65710fc-5e2a-5559-b79e-93861e08b34e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-2x-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314865} {:answer/id #uuid "244e548b-2fb8-500f-a108-39cd456a970b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{2}-x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314866} {:answer/id #uuid "b52d573b-81a2-51c7-8163-7bb56f844deb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314867}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b52d573b-81a2-51c7-8163-7bb56f844deb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314867} :answer-field/id #uuid "18dffca6-b990-50d2-8e7f-2a26d9453908" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314862}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "203b8faf-aa8f-5bc8-8c68-2ac25460b3aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-114879" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}-2x+1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\  & ↓ & 3 & 1 \\\\  & 3 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{2}-2x+1}{x-1}=3x+1+\\frac{2}{x-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}-2x+1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3x+1+\\frac{2}{x-1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314868 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator Contains a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f653e82-13d0-54e1-bd07-0e39840726b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{11}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{7}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314870} {:answer/id #uuid "a2dd0056-0de0-52ae-98b1-6e8c055fa2ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-\\frac{13}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{5}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314871} {:answer/id #uuid "b07adba2-af32-5eed-b5ee-f2a3af2eb6b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\frac{7}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{5}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314872} {:answer/id #uuid "d676c07a-2c0b-5e82-8d20-961e7ff5d295" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\frac{17}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{7}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314873} {:answer/id #uuid "7f8483fc-fe41-5200-9dbe-866b108118b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-\\frac{17}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{7}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314874}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f8483fc-fe41-5200-9dbe-866b108118b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-\\frac{17}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{7}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314874} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a66baea-5fb6-50af-a550-e2605aa07c9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314869}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0a47a19d-1921-5357-895e-fb0a72629e4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-114892" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3x-4}{2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $2$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3x-4}{2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3x-4}{2(x+\\frac{3}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3x-4}{(x+\\frac{3}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} & 3 & -4 \\\\  & ↓ & -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & 3 & -\\frac{17}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x-4}{(x+\\frac{3}{2})} & =3-\\frac{(\\frac{17}{2})}{(x+\\frac{3}{2})} \\\\  & =3-\\frac{17}{2(x+\\frac{3}{2})} \\\\  & =3-\\frac{17}{2x+3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3x-4}{2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(3-\\frac{17}{2x+3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[3{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}x-17{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[3x-\\frac{17}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[3(2-0)-\\frac{17}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2(2)+3|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2(0)+3|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[6-\\frac{17}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡7-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[6-\\frac{17}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{7}{3})] \\\\  & =3-\\frac{17}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{7}{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314875 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator Contains a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0948f21f-5869-5563-81ca-a8ca27a6796c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}[1-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314877} {:answer/id #uuid "221c19cb-0523-57d0-b722-73c15d635554" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}[1-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314878} {:answer/id #uuid "07d23c95-2369-5cbf-8fbc-7e0bd7387b68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314879} {:answer/id #uuid "703b2b05-c249-5636-a9c7-abdc4bc16f73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}[2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314880} {:answer/id #uuid "e3da8ac1-dd09-5222-9142-60c214c5338a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[2-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314881}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0948f21f-5869-5563-81ca-a8ca27a6796c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}[1-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314877} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee1680ad-2ab3-5ea4-b389-42d35cfcf513" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314876}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "349a53dd-d24d-57f8-9b3f-ad7d5c48d97a" :question/math-academy-id "q-114898" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}\\frac{8x+1}{4x-1}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $4$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}\\frac{8x+1}{4x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}\\frac{8x+1}{4(x-\\frac{1}{4})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}\\frac{8x+1}{(x-\\frac{1}{4})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} & 8 & 1 \\\\  & ↓ & 2 \\\\  & 8 & 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8x+1}{(x-\\frac{1}{4})} & =8+\\frac{3}{(x-\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =8+\\frac{12}{4x-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}\\frac{8x+1}{4x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}(8+\\frac{12}{4x-1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[8{\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}\\text{d}x+12{\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}\\frac{1}{4x-1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[8x+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x-1|]_{-1/8}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[8(0-(-\\frac{1}{8}))+3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4(0)-1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4(-\\frac{1}{8})-1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[8(\\frac{1}{8})+3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2}))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[1-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314882 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f110daa3-fd31-5e34-8a88-0e002c2e418a" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator is Linear"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cfbefb0-1e7d-58bd-88d6-a4c41d5a49af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314884}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3cfbefb0-1e7d-58bd-88d6-a4c41d5a49af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314884} :answer-field/id #uuid "4818e830-08f2-554f-9402-1d79ba7f7d3d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314883}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5fe6f2fa-cc5e-5c73-ad78-fa9e31680504" :question/math-academy-id "q-347423" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+3x-2}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-2$ | $3$ | $8$ | $3$ | $-2$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-6$ | $-4$ | $2$ |\n|  | $3$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+3x-2}{x+2}=3{x}^{2}+2x-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+3x-2}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(3{x}^{2}+2x-1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+2{\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}{|}_{0}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{|}_{0}^{2}-x{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{3}{|}_{0}^{2}+{x}^{2}{|}_{0}^{2}-x{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =[{2}^{3}-{0}^{3}]+[{2}^{2}-{0}^{2}]-[2-0] \\\\  & =8+4-2 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314885 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236f51c2-22ad-551f-afb4-62fd6de6d21e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Quotient of Linear Polynomials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4932558f-8cba-51b5-9103-a164a6b96baf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314887} {:answer/id #uuid "f1b573f4-6bae-5027-9d0d-b8e68db20675" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1b573f4-6bae-5027-9d0d-b8e68db20675" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314888} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc72520c-b6e5-56cb-ba39-46564ef3aa31" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314886} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "283bc39d-2c97-579f-947b-fc46b5877a67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "283bc39d-2c97-579f-947b-fc46b5877a67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314890} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dd706bb-8b45-5779-99a3-859e22dd8650" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314889}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "40821fd7-459c-5f1a-b598-66814fd41eb8" :question/math-academy-id "q-352216" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{7x+4}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}} $-\\,3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $7$ | $4$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-7$ |\n|  | $7$ | $-3$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{7x+4}{x+1}=7-\\frac{3}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{7x+4}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(7-\\frac{3}{x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =7{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}x-3{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =7x\\,{|}_{0}^{2}-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|\\,{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =7(2-0)-3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0+1|) \\\\  & =14-3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1) \\\\  & =14-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,3\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314891 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f110daa3-fd31-5e34-8a88-0e002c2e418a" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator is Linear"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2c5787d-d7e3-5c45-88f6-9f602635fd03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314893} {:answer/id #uuid "0084de06-a6d0-541b-b334-13d2ae825c01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314894}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2c5787d-d7e3-5c45-88f6-9f602635fd03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314893} :answer-field/id #uuid "5699bfe5-3b47-5cd8-ba8e-9f9e32c6dbb5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314892} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b253819-013c-5d7e-97cb-922d405d2e74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314896}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b253819-013c-5d7e-97cb-922d405d2e74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314896} :answer-field/id #uuid "51adb47e-4040-53ad-b1d8-8b01c644e36d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314895}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ba1ca2cd-3164-58aa-80ce-61d1bd84a956" :question/math-academy-id "q-352251" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+2x+5}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}}\n$+\\,\\,5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-2$ | $1$ | $3$ | $2$ | $5$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-2$ | $-2$ | $0$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ | $0$ | $5$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+2x+5}{x+2}={x}^{2}+x+\\frac{5}{x+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+2x+5}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+x+\\frac{5}{x+2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x+5{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}{|}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}{|}_{0}^{1}+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{2}+5(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,\\frac{3}{2}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314897 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236f51c2-22ad-551f-afb4-62fd6de6d21e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Quotient of Linear Polynomials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3a30f90-4032-5a5d-84d8-8d99dd2e794e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314899} {:answer/id #uuid "7ab79d01-9573-54f3-be11-bf963846b25d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314900} {:answer/id #uuid "c14eeb30-48b1-5164-ad1a-91805dff0bbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314901} {:answer/id #uuid "c067cf5b-0286-5c6c-b102-8e02634c4b3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314902} {:answer/id #uuid "1d99632e-994b-5695-b0aa-7e0158559c4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d99632e-994b-5695-b0aa-7e0158559c4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314903} :answer-field/id #uuid "b26ab68d-a2a4-508c-a468-e0734cd5550c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314898}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fdc1997e-1bad-55a9-b760-1b70db782f65" :question/math-academy-id "q-49353" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{2x-3}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\  & ↓ & 2 \\\\  & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{2x-3}{x-1}=2-\\frac{1}{x-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{2x-3}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}(2-\\frac{1}{x-1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}2\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x{|}_{2}^{3}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|{|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =2(3-2)-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3-1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2-1|) \\\\  & =2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314904 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236f51c2-22ad-551f-afb4-62fd6de6d21e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Quotient of Linear Polynomials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6aec6078-01a4-5b59-93d5-68b741df2d28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314906} {:answer/id #uuid "49eaa986-5e8a-5ee8-bfcb-04d71b74d6fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314907} {:answer/id #uuid "43207d35-a11f-5227-b363-5116699634ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314908} {:answer/id #uuid "6e7bc3a5-251e-5de7-9737-1b55ced5e7a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314909} {:answer/id #uuid "3e35a6e5-48f5-5ec7-92a6-fa0e877d97c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x+7\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314910}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43207d35-a11f-5227-b363-5116699634ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314908} :answer-field/id #uuid "585def09-c78b-5de6-9b00-3dbc3c05e2dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314905}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8994c3eb-f396-5b4f-a637-dc6bb7953e49" :question/math-academy-id "q-49354" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{5x+7}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -2 & 5 & 7 \\\\  & ↓ & -10 \\\\  & 5 & -3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{5x+7}{x+2}=5-\\frac{3}{x+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5x+7}{x+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (5-\\frac{3}{x+2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\int \\text{d}x-3\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314911 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236f51c2-22ad-551f-afb4-62fd6de6d21e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Quotient of Linear Polynomials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61f4887b-3d01-58b1-bcd9-d2fb19997842" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314913} {:answer/id #uuid "2e147fd6-0f93-5c00-8018-d07ef10f0ae8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314914} {:answer/id #uuid "2708a6b9-fb75-5c92-9425-f57e1167c066" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314915} {:answer/id #uuid "8f75d583-8a2e-5cf8-a698-0af2fdc387f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314916} {:answer/id #uuid "c248c35d-9a92-551e-802d-626ecaaa5da8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314917}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2708a6b9-fb75-5c92-9425-f57e1167c066" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314915} :answer-field/id #uuid "461040fd-6236-57ff-af4a-4babd622bde1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314912}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fef7e5a4-8743-520c-8404-5503ee85f90a" :question/math-academy-id "q-49398" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\frac{x+4}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -3 & 1 & 4 \\\\  & ↓ & -3 \\\\  & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+4}{x+3}=1+\\frac{1}{x+3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\frac{x+4}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}(1+\\frac{1}{x+3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{|}_{-2}^{0}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|{|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =(0-(-2))+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0+3|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|-2+3|) \\\\  & =2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314918 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236f51c2-22ad-551f-afb4-62fd6de6d21e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Quotient of Linear Polynomials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9f73465-12f9-54bb-9b1f-951bde5354fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314920} {:answer/id #uuid "73c1b4b2-a28d-52e3-9ad0-dfc0fef5e959" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+7\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314921} {:answer/id #uuid "d930ceeb-c9bd-5095-9fc0-024166487bbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314922} {:answer/id #uuid "cc159f6d-d5a9-5271-aaf6-ecec47b452fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314923} {:answer/id #uuid "3cfac6be-6ca6-52fe-9829-e171e5e3356e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314924}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73c1b4b2-a28d-52e3-9ad0-dfc0fef5e959" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+7\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314921} :answer-field/id #uuid "44395535-a76b-5c25-844b-25b0e90ae2da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314919}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5d0aa088-8659-5147-af8c-f3e690e90bb6" :question/math-academy-id "q-49404" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{x+3}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\  & ↓ & 4 \\\\  & 1 & 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+3}{x-4}=1+\\frac{7}{x-4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x+3}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (1+\\frac{7}{x-4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\text{d}x+7\\int \\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x+7\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314925 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f110daa3-fd31-5e34-8a88-0e002c2e418a" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator is Linear"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40cfe201-9787-508c-8e70-b0596683b0da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314927} {:answer/id #uuid "1ba9139d-9490-5d2b-8385-69b3e7d3faab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314928} {:answer/id #uuid "5426e042-f327-5f9f-ac58-a808fb35adb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314929} {:answer/id #uuid "84763b15-40f1-5825-b82e-26fe15468bb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}+3x-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314930} {:answer/id #uuid "25598e22-6f0a-5255-920d-f516cc74ae91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}+9x-16\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25598e22-6f0a-5255-920d-f516cc74ae91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}+9x-16\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314931} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0524d15-486e-578f-914b-d6f592515942" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314926}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3542045d-f5df-5dac-bdce-4e5e5781c7c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-49421" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-x+2}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 & -1 & 2 \\\\  & ↓ & -2 & 10 & -18 \\\\  & 1 & -5 & 9 & -16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-x+2}{x+2}={x}^{2}-5x+9-\\frac{16}{x+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-x+2}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({x}^{2}-5x+9-\\frac{16}{x+2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+9\\int \\text{d}x-16\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}+9x-16\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314932 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f110daa3-fd31-5e34-8a88-0e002c2e418a" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator is Linear"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b57d584-29e0-514d-8ce7-8bf95af333ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314934} {:answer/id #uuid "0dcd9336-343a-59a5-ae33-3e75a9e8f1de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-3x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314935} {:answer/id #uuid "953549fb-6843-5e38-a909-0b2d32bb2e7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{9}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314936} {:answer/id #uuid "66c47afb-0399-5e9b-bb15-85438050f36b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+2x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314937} {:answer/id #uuid "ca0308f5-8d24-5bea-8cea-4b6d5f17f3ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314938}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b57d584-29e0-514d-8ce7-8bf95af333ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314934} :answer-field/id #uuid "06777435-7464-543f-9a23-0ac5af9f8489" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314933}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1b477fe5-67ac-5170-be29-6f6d97baa23e" :question/math-academy-id "q-49456" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{3{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+x-1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ 3 & 3 & -9 & 1 & -1 \\\\  & ↓ & 9 & 0 & 3 \\\\  & 3 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+x-1}{x-3}=3{x}^{2}+1+\\frac{2}{x-3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+x-1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{x}^{2}+1+\\frac{2}{x-3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{3}+x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064784 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator Contains a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6ec7aa7-5704-5568-870c-5ce10aacd246" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063215} {:answer/id #uuid "0696118c-8d16-57bc-84f9-e194e1db5ed6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 + 4\\ln 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063216} {:answer/id #uuid "07a57a23-ffe8-5b87-b518-04162c920b8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063217} {:answer/id #uuid "3ab8157c-2a73-5169-9c52-b0b3c1080178" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2} + 3\\ln 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063218} {:answer/id #uuid "6eb36860-7c3a-5cc7-a89a-742e3848ffba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 - \\frac{7}{4}\\ln 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6eb36860-7c3a-5cc7-a89a-742e3848ffba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 - \\frac{7}{4}\\ln 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063219} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bff75e6-1700-5d80-adcb-dc6641c8c8b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063214}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1aaedd48-8858-5316-b8f3-55fab9e40276" :question/math-academy-id "q-49467" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x-1}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $2$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x-1}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x-1}{2(x+\\frac{1}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x-1}{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $5$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-\\frac{5}{2}$ |\n|  | $5$ | $-\\frac{7}{2}$ |\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5x-1}{(x+\\frac{1}{2})} & =5-\\frac{(\\frac{7}{2})}{(x+\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =5-\\frac{7}{2(x+\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =5-\\frac{7}{2x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x-1}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(5-\\frac{7}{2x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[5{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}x-7{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[5x{|}_{0}^{2}-\\frac{7}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|{|}_{0}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[5(2-0)-\\frac{7}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2\\cdot 2+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2\\cdot 0+1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[10-\\frac{7}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5] \\\\  & =5-\\frac{7}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314939 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator Contains a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a31a2406-8c00-544b-b546-9fb5a6cb8839" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-9\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x-2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314941} {:answer/id #uuid "c8ede3df-b267-5dc0-8d33-5cf94aec0675" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x-2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314942} {:answer/id #uuid "06f32f5a-d56c-5081-84b4-dca0e328942e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x-2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314943} {:answer/id #uuid "d3f2d779-8c3a-54e5-81ce-1ea0aabe1568" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x-2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314944} {:answer/id #uuid "d19b9b0e-b55f-5ab1-82ad-89e1f137dde2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+9\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x-2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314945}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3f2d779-8c3a-54e5-81ce-1ea0aabe1568" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x-2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314944} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf83b17d-180d-56c4-973a-30baa98fb981" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314940}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5f43a9f2-6f72-5d1e-8a03-5c7d7f915857" :question/math-academy-id "q-73391" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{x-1}{3x-2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $3$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-1}{3x-2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{x-1}{3(x-\\frac{2}{3})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{x-1}{(x-\\frac{2}{3})}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 1 & -1 \\\\  & ↓ & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & 1 & -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-1}{(x-\\frac{2}{3})} & =1+\\frac{(-\\frac{1}{3})}{(x-\\frac{2}{3})} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{3(x-\\frac{2}{3})} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{3x-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-1}{3x-2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int (1-\\frac{1}{3x-2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\int \\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{1}{3x-2}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[x-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x-2|]+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x-2|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314946 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator Contains a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "838ede82-8ed2-5ef1-aef1-e164c6498a7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314948} {:answer/id #uuid "f6fa9517-0bf4-5c5d-b3b9-6dd7502a3d13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314949} {:answer/id #uuid "00bf9bab-e697-5c8f-b378-0ddca2be3fac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{4}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314950} {:answer/id #uuid "253e0e12-fbaf-5a39-bbfb-820fa13b60d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314951} {:answer/id #uuid "1a5d29a7-90d0-55b6-b519-45be6629db78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314952}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6fa9517-0bf4-5c5d-b3b9-6dd7502a3d13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314949} :answer-field/id #uuid "a91b7c95-ab58-55b4-a6a1-00c0e9da230f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314947}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "81a5f9d4-4d33-54e5-b177-b660410e589f" :question/math-academy-id "q-73392" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{x-1}{2x+6}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $2$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-1}{2x+6}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{x-1}{2(x+3)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{x-1}{(x+3)}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -3 & 1 & -1 \\\\  & ↓ & -3 \\\\  & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-1}{(x+3)} & =1+\\frac{(-4)}{(x+3)} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{4}{(x+3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-1}{2x+6}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (1-\\frac{4}{x+3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\int \\text{d}x-4\\int \\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[x-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|]+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
